{
  "requirement": "Each requirement and example declaration badge has two adjacent links. Its\nkind (`req` or `example`) links to the declaration's anchor on the current\npage; its full name links to the evidence detail page. These segments stay\ntogether in one non-wrapping row, with no separate arrow link or plaintext evidence link.\nEach detail page links back to the declaration's anchored badge and to the\nindex. Reference badges continue to link to the declaration. These links\nresolve when a requirement name contains `.md`, as in\n`requirements.cli.mdbook`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests against each clause of `requirements.index.navigation`. I did not read implementation source. I found no gap.\n\n**Two adjacent links per req/example badge**\n- `src/lib.rs` `declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies` checks, for a req and an example, that the header holds a kind link and a name link. The kind link has `href=\"#habeas-{kind}-rules.{name}\"` and the text `req` or `example`. The name link has `href=\"requirements-index/rules.{name}.html\"` and the title `View evidence for rules.{name}`.\n- `declaration_badges_and_margin_controls_share_kind_colors` and `tests/repository.rs` `mdbook_preprocessor_renders_definitions_between_stdin_and_stdout` cover the same two-link structure. The preprocessor test asserts that each `habeas-definition-badge` row has exactly two `</a>` elements, one `habeas-badge-kind` link and one `habeas-badge-name` link.\n- That preprocessor test also asserts the anchor href and the evidence href.\n\n**One non-wrapping row; no arrow link or plaintext evidence link**\n- `declaration_badge_stylesheet_keeps_split_links_in_one_row` asserts `inline-flex`, `flex-wrap: nowrap`, `white-space: nowrap` and `flex-shrink: 0` on the wrapper and its links.\n- `declaration_sections_contain_their_headers_and_markdown_bodies` asserts that the header has no `habeas-detail-icon`.\n- Other tests assert no `<svg` in the badge and no `See evidence` text.\n\n**Detail pages link back to the anchored badge and to the index**\n- `src/index.rs` `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` asserts the `[View definition](../../requirements/core.html#habeas-req-...)` link and the `[Requirements index](../requirements-index.html)` link.\n- `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` checks every detail page's index link, including nested chapters (`../rules/child.html#...`).\n- `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` covers an example declaration and an index placed in a subdirectory.\n- `detail_pages_link_to_readme_chapters_at_their_index_output` covers README chapters.\n\n**Reference badges still link to the declaration**\n- `references_in_nested_chapters_link_to_the_requirement_definition` asserts, for the impl, cite and test badges in a nested chapter, an `href=\"../requirements.html#habeas-req-requirements.ready\"`.\n\n**Names containing `.md`**\n- `links_preserve_requirement_names_containing_md` asserts the encoded detail-page href and the encoded definition-anchor href.\n- `definitions_without_a_marker_get_a_default_index_and_detail_pages` checks the `rules.cli.mdbook` kind anchor, name link and View-definition link. `index_owns_details_in_book_order_with_badge_icons` checks the example `more.cli.mdbook` links.\n- `links_to_readme_chapters_use_the_index_output` covers `chapter_href` for README chapters.\n\nTest-marking is adequate: the relevant tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.",
  "references": "c695497dc38e4a206fcdcbcdf19c6f99199afeef8d23c602364dc4aeef8b31d6",
